592186377695 #edb/ref 1069 "q-74920" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186377695 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186377695 #edb/ref 1071 "Find  ${lim}_{x\\to (1,-3)}\\frac{xy-y}{x-1}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186377695 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9d22711b-d1d6-5f06-ab4a-74275f71d77c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186377695 #edb/ref 1074 "Attempting to evaluate the limit by direct substitution leads to the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0},$ as follows: \n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (1,-3)}\\frac{xy-y}{x-1}=\\frac{1\\cdot (-3)-(-3)}{1-1}=\\frac{0}{0}\n$$\n\nHowever, we can simplify the limit by canceling common factors in the numerator and denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (1,-3)}\\frac{xy-y}{x-1} & ={lim}_{x\\to (1,-3)}\\frac{(x-1)y}{x-1} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to (1,-3)}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the limit has been simplified, we can evaluate it using direct substitution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (1,-3)}y & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the limit evaluates to $-3.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186377696 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377697 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186377696 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377698 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186377696 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377699 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186377696 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377700 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186377696 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377701 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186377696 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186377696 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186377696 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186377699 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186377696 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "117ca5de-bfde-5504-8e9b-162dc1ee9296" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186377697 #edb/ref 1080 "3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186377697 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186377697 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3d118fc5-1c52-5566-be98-a9707e774937" #